message: "If you use this research, code, or benchmark in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Comparative Analysis of Advanced CNN Architectures for Multi-Class Brain Tumor Classification Using MRI"
abstract: >-
  Early detection and planning for treatment of brain tumors is essential and is facilitated
  by magnetic resonance imaging (MRI). Manual reading of MRI is labor intensive and can be
  subject to mistakes since various types of tumors share similar visual features. In this
  research, a deep learning system for the classification of brain tumors into multiple
  classes (glioma, meningioma, pituitary, and normal brain) using MRI images is presented.
  Tumor classification was performed using advanced pre-trained deep learning architectures
  employing transfer learning and fine-tuning: EfficientNetV2, DenseNet121, and ResNet50V2.
  Experimental results demonstrated that EfficientNetV2 achieved 98.92% accuracy, the best
  Macro-AUC score of 0.9999, and the lowest misclassification rate. Grad-CAM visualization
  was employed to verify spatial interpretability and clinical relevance.
